#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# key_sort_by

#% text
# `key_sort_by(a, f)` gives the association `a` (or the association of a list of rules) with its entries in the canonical order of `f(key)`. `key_sort_by(f)(a)` is the operator form.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
key_sort_by(assoc(2 -> a, 3 -> b, 1 -> c), k => mod(k, 3))
#% output
#= assoc(3 -> b, 1 -> c, 2 -> a)

#% cell
key_sort_by(["aaa" -> 1, "ab" -> 2, "abcd" -> 3], string_length)
#% output
#= assoc("ab" -> 2, "aaa" -> 1, "abcd" -> 3)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `key_sort`, `sort_by`
